19:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"listener"}]," currently has exactly one variant, ",["$","code",null,{"children":"http"}],", which serves\nHTTP/HTTP2 and therefore gRPC. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"socket_address"}]," is parsed as a Rust\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"SocketAddr"}],", so it must be an IP literal plus port: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"0.0.0.0:50051"}]," to bind\nevery IPv4 interface, ",["$","code",null,{"children":"[::]:50051"}]," for IPv6, ",["$","code",null,{"children":"127.0.0.1:50051"}]," for loopback\nonly. A hostname or a bare ",["$","code",null,{"children":":port"}]," is rejected as an invalid address. TLS,\nHTTP/2 tuning, and compression are options on the listener, not on the\nservices."]}]
