21:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"capabilities"}]," is the one that surprises people: it carries almost no config,\nbut Bazel queries it before doing anything else and fails the build if the\ncall is not served, with an error about querying capabilities rather than one\nnaming a missing service. And if ",["$","code",null,{"children":"capabilities"}]," has no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"remote_execution"}],"\nblock, the response carries no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"execution_capabilities"}],", so the client is\ntold this endpoint caches but does not execute, which is correct for a\ncache-only Getting started deployment and a silent bug once you add Remote\nexecution."]}]
