2d:["$","p",null,{"children":["A client calling the CAS can upload and fetch blobs. A worker connected to the\nworker API is ",["$","em",null,{"children":"handed actions to execute"}]," and reports their results as\nauthoritative. Those are not the same permission, and the worker API has no\nauthentication of its own to distinguish them."]}]
2e:["$","p",null,{"children":["The rule: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_api"}]," gets its own listener, on its own port, with no\nother service sharing it."]}]," The shipped examples put the public API on\n",["$","code",null,{"children":":50051"}]," and the worker API on ",["$","code",null,{"children":":50061"}],", and the second port is the one you\nnever expose beyond the cluster:"]}]
