39:["$","$L60",null,{"children":[["$","$L61",null,{"title":"Can one process have more than two servers?","id":"can-one-process-have-more-than-two-servers","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["Yes; the array is unbounded, and separating concerns by port is the intended\nuse. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"deployment-examples/docker-compose/local-storage-cas.json5"}]," serves the\nsame cache twice, plain on ",["$","code",null,{"children":":50051"}]," and TLS on ",["$","code",null,{"children":":50071"}],". A third listener for\nbuild events, or a plain-HTTP health endpoint a load balancer can probe\nwithout TLS, follows the same pattern."]}]}],["$","$L61",null,{"title":"Why is `bytestream` separate from `cas`?","id":"why-is-bytestream-separate-from-cas","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["REAPI splits them deliberately. The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cas"}]," service handles batched reads and\nwrites of small blobs; the ByteStream service streams large ones. Bazel\nstrongly prefers the streaming interface for anything sizeable, so a cache\nthat serves ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cas"}]," but not ",["$","code",null,{"children":"bytestream"}]," will appear to work and then fail on\nyour first large artifact. Point both at the same store."]}]}],["$","$L61",null,{"title":"What does the `admin` service actually do?","id":"what-does-the-admin-service-actually-do","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["It exposes a small REST endpoint for administrative operations at a\nconfigurable path, defaulting to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/admin"}],". It is not an authenticated control\nplane; it belongs on the private port with the worker API, not on anything\nreachable from outside the cluster."]}]}],["$","$L61",null,{"title":"Do I need `health` if I have a load balancer?","id":"do-i-need-health-if-i-have-a-load-balancer","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["You need it ",["$","em",null,{"children":"because"}]," you have a load balancer. It serves ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/status"}]," by default\nand takes a ",["$","code",null,{"children":"timeout_seconds"}]," for the checks it runs. Without it, a probe can\nonly test whether the port accepts a TCP connection, which stays true long\nafter a process has stopped being useful."]}]}],["$","$L61",null,{"title":"I set `read_only: true` on the action cache. What does that stop?","id":"i-set-read_only-true-on-the-action-cache-what-does-that-stop","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"Clients can read cached action results but cannot write new ones. It's the\nright setting for an endpoint you expose to untrusted or unverified builds\n(they benefit from the cache without being able to poison it) while a trusted\nCI endpoint on a different port writes to the same store."}]}]]}]
